''               t0-stopmode 16,611 -> 8,529 bytes. No record's text changes.
''               23 Sep 2026 -- task 3613, SRC_REV 12: a hand row waits for the hand. At Visit 10 every hand
''               row ended before Stephen touched the wheel. A hold row's watch bound ran from START, so
''               rows 1 and 2 ended 2 s and 3 s after START. A coast row's 400 ms rest test counted from
''               START, so a wheel not yet spun read as at rest. Now a hold row's bound runs from the
''               first displacement, and a coast row can end at rest only after its first hall tick.
''               Before that, only DONE, ABORT or the 120 s T0_24_HAND_CAP_MS ends a row.
''               24 Sep 2026 -- task 3617, SRC_REV 13 (PL-123, VISIT-10-PASS2-EVALUATION.md SS3.6). Four
''               instrument fixes to T0-24, one per PL-123 item:
''               (1) Each hold row re-arms the hold before it runs (bT0sRearmHold(): SM_FLOAT for
''               T0_24_REARM_MS, then SM_BRAKE again), and is set up only when getHoldStatus() then reads
''               HS_HOLDING at displacement 0 with no fault signal. The watch's first sample must read the
''               same, or the row's cell is NOMEAS. New record T0-24,row,N,rearm; hold_result gains
''               start_hs, start_disp and start_held.
''               (2) The half-rate time is replaced by a speed-invariant reading: band_ticks, the hall ticks
''               the wheel carries from T0_24_BAND_RATE (120 ticks/s) to rest. The band is fixed and the same
''               for every row, so the reading does not depend on how fast the wheel was spun or driven. A
''               row released below the band is NOMEAS (in_band FALSE). The limits are re-derived from the
''               logs on record (CON { T0-24 sign-off limits }). The numeric cells now print units TICKS,
''               and the seven stop cells' criterion tokens are renamed to say so. Every six-tick span now covers six tick
''               intervals, one electrical cycle. Up to SRC_REV 12, t0sProbe() and t0sMeasureSteadyRate()
''               covered five, so their release_span_ms values in older logs are five intervals. The coast
''               row no longer reads the panel's input or redraws it while the wheel is turning. Each such
''               read stops the hall poll for about 30 ms, and at speed that dropped ticks. Records: the
''               coast record and the row record replace half_ms with band_ticks, band_ms and in_band.
''               The coast record also gains band_span_ms and band_entered, and at_rest gains band_entered.
''               (3) The fault rows force the fault with testForceFault() (DRIVER_REV 12+) under FR_SHIPPED,
''               not the offset shift, which plugged the motor instead (PL-119, pass 2 aborted at 10.4 A).
''               The provoke record changes shape. The rows end with testResetFault(), because
''               DCS_FAULTED is a latch since DRIVER_REV 14.
''               (4) The panel names the wheel, RIGHT WHEEL (P16 BOARD), from the first screen on. The
''               window title carries it, and so does the header art (tools/gen_t0stop_assets.py
''               HEADER_TEXT).
''               Same task, the arbiter's ruling on the first round (P7: nothing silent):
''               The art is regenerated. The fault row under SM_BRAKE is labelled "FAULT, BRAKE MODE",
''               since "hold" means only the hold at rest. The spin rows ask for a HARD spin that must
''               pass the measuring speed. A spin row whose try is not measured shows a TOO SLOW cell
''               that keeps the row's prediction, and it is tried again, up to T0_24_SPIN_TRIES (3)
''               (t0sRunSpinRow(), record T0-24,row,N,try). Only then, or when DONE / ABORT ended a try,
''               is it NOMEAS, on a screen that says why (T0_24_ACT_SPIN_NOMEAS). The E-STOP row is spun
''               FREE, and t0sProbe() applies emergencyCutoff() at the band-entry tick: a hand cannot
''               spin a shorted wheel into the band (pass 2 reached 22.5 ticks/s). It counts only when
''               the short was applied there and latched. The coast record gains shorted.
''               t0sBandTick() enters the band only after a release above it.
''               24 Sep 2026 -- task 3619, SRC_REV 14 (PL-127, DOCs/plans/T0-24-INTERACTION-DESIGN.md): T0-24's
''               interaction is rebuilt as a lesson. Stephen, at pass 3: rows moved on without him, the
''               panel did not say enough, DONE and ABORT did nothing, and there was no way to redo a row.
''               - Every row runs INTRO (a preview, then START ROW) -> SETUP -> ACT -> RESULT. A hand row's
''                 ACT ends only on DONE or ABORT, never on a timer: the hold rows' watch bounds and the
''                 120 s cap are gone, and a spin row takes as many spins as he gives it (each a logged try;
''                 the SPIN_TRIES limit is gone). Setup and the two powered rows end by themselves.
''               - The RESULT screen stays until NEXT ROW (FINISH on the last) or REDO ROW. A redo re-runs
''                 the row's setup and ACT; the cells use each row's last run.
''               - Only live buttons are drawn: the forward action in the right slot, ABORT or REDO in the
''                 left. Enter and Esc duplicate them; S, D and SPACE are retired.
''               - Cog 0 is the panel, and polls PC_MOUSE on every pass (~30 ms), because a click is a live
''                 button state. A new measure cog (t0sWorker()) owns the hall poll, the hold samples and
''                 every timed act, and prints nothing. Its tries and hold samples are printed by cog 0
''                 after each step, so the hold_log lines now carry ms and arrive after the row.
''               - New records: T0-24,screen / status / input (every press, with the button it chose,
''                 MISS or IGNORED) / cogs / row,N,run,K,result. The row and hold_result records gain run.
''               - The art is eight layers from tools/gen_t0stop_assets.py, which also prints the screen
''                 table t0sScreenTab that picks each (row, phase)'s banner, card, labels and buttons, and
''                 renders every screen with --storyboard for the desk review.
''               24 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV 15 (PL-128): the window title loses its parentheses. At src_rev 14 the ')' of
''               '(P16 BOARD)' closed the debug() call, the rest of the line became a comment, and the window opened at
''               the host's default size, a quarter of the panel. No record changes.
''               24 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV 16 (PL-130, PL-131): HOLD-RISE judges the hold's rise from its rate while
''               displaced (rise_ms, new on the hold_start record), in 220-280 ms, not the wall time from his first
''               push; a slip or limit after the ceiling no longer fails it. Its res1 is rise_ms. Rows 1, 4 and 6
''               ask on the panel for the three deliberate acts (the empty-panel click, a REDO, an ABORT).
''               25 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV 17 (PL-134, PL-135): HOLD-RISE's rate counts a pair only while getHoldStatus()
''               reads HS_HOLDING at both ends; and the three acts are REQUIRED on their row's first run by a screen
''               drawing only the control that performs each (t0sTestTab): row 1's grey box, row 4's and row 6's REDO,
''               row 6's ABORT. The screen record gains panel_test.
''               25 Sep 2026 -- task 3621 (R20.1 part 3), SRC_REV 18: the driver's reporting (DRIVER-REPORTING-DESIGN.md
''               SS6). New build -D T0_STOPREASON (tier t0-stopreason, UNATTENDED, the RIGHT wheel driven at power 15):
''               T0-25 runs the four stop-reason legs and the event-log checks -- R20-T0-SR-COMMANDED, -SR-ATLIMIT,
''               -SR-ESTOP, -SR-LINKLOST, R20-T0-EV-STOP, -EV-LOST, -EV-TOTAL and -EV-2COG. New records T0-25,leg / ev /
''               lost / total / twocog. T0_ATTENDED becomes T0_OWN_TIER: it compiles the unattended bodies out of every
''               build that runs one test of its own, which now includes an unattended one. T0-24 (t0-stopmode) gains
''               R20-T0-EV-HOLD: after each hold row's ACT, cog 0 reads the event log, and the hand-offs it reports must
''               match the hold states the measure cog saw. New record T0-24,row,N,run,K,events.
''               26 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV 19 (Visit 10 pass 5, task 3613): pass 5's T0-25 was voided when PL-120 left the
''               right bridge dead and start() refused it. A RIGHT start refused by its checks now prints T0-25,refused
''               and three T0-25,rprobe (the last attempt's lead-check mV), then T0-25 starts the LEFT wheel
''               (T0_SECOND_BASE, T0-25,fallback) and its cells name LEFT. Nothing else changes.
''               26 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV 20 (Visit 10 pass 6, task 3613): pass 6's first load refused the right again (PL-120)
''               and it was back within 2 min. After a refused right and the LEFT's cells, T0-25 now times its return:
''               one start of the right every T0_25_REC_GAP_MS (10 s) for up to T0_25_REC_MAX_MS (3 min), each printed
''               T0-25,recover (try, ms since the refusal) with its T0-25,refused or T0-25,health and rprobe lines, then
''               T0-25,recovered (ms, or NA). The tier runs up to about 3 minutes longer only when the right is refused.
''               26 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV 21 (PL-151, T0 half): two API promises with no cell gain one, each able to FAIL, run
''               after R20-T0-EV-2COG so the seven legs' EV-STOP read and EV-TOTAL's 27 are untouched. R20-T0-ROTSTOP:
''               stopAfterRotation(T0_25_ROT_TURNS, DRU_ROTATIONS) from a reset tracking, then the drive, reads SR_AT_LIMIT
''               at rest within T0_25_ROT_TOL_TICKS of the limit; NEGATIVE, the same drive with nothing armed does not stop
''               by itself in that window plus T0_25_ROT_NEG_EXTRA_MS and runs past the limit (records T0-25,rotstop and
''               T0-25,rotstop_neg). R20-T0-ESTOPSTATUS: getStatus() at rest is not DS_ESTOP, reads DS_ESTOP after
''               emergencyCutoff() and not after clearEmergency() (record T0-25,estopstatus). A start that does not
''               come up leaves both NOMEAS, as the other eight.
''               26 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV 22 (DRIVER_REV 33/34; PL-153, PL-155, PL-156, PL-158, PL-159): three T0-25 cells
''               run after R20-T0-ESTOPSTATUS, the existing ten and the EV-STOP sequence untouched. R20-T0-ODOMETER: two
''               back-to-back driveForDistance() moves each travel their own distance within T0_25_ROT_TOL_TICKS, and the
''               odometer (getRotationCount(), getDistance()) is unchanged across an emergencyCutoff()/clearEmergency()
''               held T0_25_ESTOP_HOLD_MS (record T0-25,odometer). R20-T0-MOVEDONE: isMoveDone() is FALSE as the move
''               is accepted, TRUE at rest after it and TRUE while e-stopped (record T0-25,movedone). R20-T0-PERSIST:
''               max speeds, the hold and the reversal set with the motor stopped read back after a restart, and the
''               hold is in force (record T0-25,persist). New build -D T0_API (tier t0-api): T0-26, the API contract --
''               every value-taking setter's boundaries accepted and read back, the values just outside refused with
''               their ERR_* and nothing changed, settings made before start() kept, calibrate() not implemented; one
''               cell per method family, each counting its bad calls, with a T0-26,chk record per call. Wheels up,
''               unattended, no motion (records T0-26,*).
''               26 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV 23 (DRIVER_REV 35; PL-160, user half): T0-26 checks setDeceleration(). In
''               R20-T0-API-ACCEL: its boundaries [DECEL_MIN_MM_S2 .. DECEL_MAX_MM_S2] accepted and read back through
''               getDeceleration(), the values just outside (and 0, -1) refused with ERR_BAD_COUNT and the ramp and both
''               getters unchanged; setAcceleration()'s rows now also read back through getAcceleration(); and a set
''               deceleration reaches the driver -- on the running motor getRampingValues()'s decrRamp equals the step
''               this file converts the rate to (T0A_DECEL_PROBE), and lands within 1% of the built-in 50_000 for the
''               rate that step gives (T0A_DECEL_ANCHOR). In R20-T0-API-PERSIST: setAcceleration() and setDeceleration()
''               made with the motor stopped read back after each start() and the restart, and the kept deceleration is
''               the driver's decrRamp. No new debug() record: every check is a T0-26,chk.
''               27 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV 24 (PL-14, PL-51, PL-52): three fixes with no certifying check gain one, each
''               able to FAIL. PL-14, in R20-T0-API-PERSIST: a start() at another voltage the motor supports (the next
''               lower PWR_*, else the next higher) is taken, and getDriveVoltage() reads that voltage and its nominal
''               mV; a restart at DRIVE_VOLTAGE reads DRIVE_VOLTAGE again. The pre-fix library ignored the argument, so
''               it read DRIVE_VOLTAGE both times. Nothing is driven. PL-51, in R20-T0-API-STEER: steer's
''               setMaxSpeedForDistance() per t0aSpeedTab reads back through steer.getMaxSpeedForDistance(), with the
''               max speed left at its default 75, so the defect (it returned getMaxSpeed()) fails every row but the
''               last. PL-52, in R20-T0-SR-COMMANDED (T0-25, already driving): getPower() reads T0_25_POWER as the
''               COMMANDED leg drives and 0 after its stopMotor() (new record T0-25,power); the pre-fix getPower()
''               still read 15 after the stop. T0-26 stays motionless.
''               27 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV 25 (DRIVER_REV 38, PL-160): the jerk-limited ramp generator. NEW in T0-25
''               (t0-stopreason), after R20-T0-MOVEDONE and before R20-T0-PERSIST: the wheel is driven at powers 50 and
''               25 while a sampler cog reads the driver's status run pass by pass and judges only the pairs of passes
''               it resolved (t0rRamp(), t0pWatch()). R22-T0-RAMP-SHAPE (a speed-up from rest, a slow-down, a stop:
''               every pass's acceleration within one jerk step of the last and inside its limit, none after arrival,
''               no overshoot, the stop never through zero), R22-T0-RAMP-REVERSE (a reversal crosses zero in one
''               ramp, never DCS_STOPPED), R22-T0-RAMP-UNWIND (a stop read at the speed-up's limit unwinds it at the
''               larger jerk, within RAMP_TAU_MS), R22-T0-STOPPLAN-C (stopAfterRotation() and stopAfterTime() armed
''               at cruise come to rest at their limit: the plan's stop against the stop's own ticks and ms) and
''               R22-T0-STOPPLAN-M (stopAfterDistance(), stopAfterRotation() and stopAfterTime() armed at rest fire
''               mid-ramp and come to rest at their limit). New records T0-25,rampseg, T0-25,rampend, T0-25,unwind,
''               T0-25,plan. NEW in T0-26 (t0-api): R22-T0-API-RAMPDEF, the built-in ramp -- getAcceleration()
''               ACCEL_BUILTIN_MM_S2, getDeceleration() DECEL_BUILTIN_MM_S2 and getRampingValues() the four driver
''               parameters derived from them -- before start() and on the running driver. RE-CERTIFIED: R17-T0-ACCEL
''               (t0) reads setAcceleration()'s rate as the speed-up limit with its jerk, anchored on the 6.5in
''               wheel's derived 33_958 steps for 1_000 mm/s^2 (token MM_S2_LIMIT_JERK, was MM_S2_CONST_RAMP);
''               R20-T0-API-ACCEL and R20-T0-API-PERSIST judge the four parameters as the two limits and their jerks,
''               the anchor on the derived 49_918 for DECEL_BUILTIN_MM_S2 (was 1% of the old 50_000 ramp_down).
''               DRIVER_REV 39 (PL-161, the driver plans its own stop and publishes it ~232 us after each pass, never
''               late, early by its age and its take-pass case): the sampler reads drv_accel_now by the library's
''               DRVR_STATUS_ACCEL_NOW_IDX (no longer the run's last long), and every stop-limit bound in T0-25 gains
''               the plan's early term, T0_25_PLAN_EARLY_TICKS: R20-T0-ROTSTOP and R20-T0-ODOMETER -4 .. +3 ticks
''               (were +/- 3); the new time legs -6 .. +4 ms, derived term by term in CON.
''               27 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV 26 (DRIVER_REV 39; PL-161, PL-163): two cells the release-candidate sheet
''               named as not built. NEW in T0-25 (t0-stopreason): R22-T0-FRAMESLACK (PL-161) -- DRIVER_REV 39 plans
''               the stop in the slack of the nine PWM frames after each drive pass, and its failure is a frame that
''               overruns (or loses an ADC sample). A frame watcher cog (t0fWatch()) reads the driver's loop_ticks
''               -- each control frame's ADC wait plus its own work -- on every frame for the whole of t0rRamp()'s
''               drives, stops and mid-ramp limit stops, and the cell judges the least against the frame's own work
''               bound, from frame_cnt (testGetDriveConstants()) and PL-161's per-frame work count (CON states each
''               term); new record T0-25,frame. NEW build -D T0_REVA (tier t0-reva): T0-27, R22-T0-REVA-FOLD (PL-163)
''               -- on a Rev A board, found by auto-detection on either pin group and printed, testSetCurrentLimits(2,
''               2) and a driven, unloaded wheel at the duty floor count no foldback_frames over a stated window, at
''               two powers; new records T0-27,*. No existing record or cell changes.
''               27 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV 26 extended (DRIVER_REV 40, PL-163's residual, FOLD_MIN_MV = 4): the fold's
''               own duty floor is raised so its threshold is never under 4 mV -- a fold needs a 5 mV net reading,
''               not the 1 mV this note's cell first assumed. R22-T0-REVA-FOLD is measured when the window's largest
''               duty is at or under the driver's duty_floor (read from the parameter run), and T0-27,leg gains
''               duty_floor_drv, t_eff_mv (4), net_max_mv and outcome (duty_floor is now duty_floor_est, t_floor_mv
''               is gone, lim_err/peak_a/cont_a fold into lim_ok), its sense fields moving to a new T0-27,legsense
''               (with samples) to keep each record under 255 bytes. A fold on 4 mV or less is the defect,
''               FAIL; an unloaded net reading of 5 mV falsifies the noise premise, NOMEAS with crit PREMISE_NOISE.
''               The window is read with no wait. NEW, ATTENDED: R22-T0-REVA-FOLDPOS, the positive control -- the
''               same wheel at the same 2 A limit, gripped by hand (t0reva window, SPACE, GRIP) at a duty over m = 0.2,
''               must fold on 5 mV or more; new records T0-27,hold,prompt, T0-27,holdsense and T0-27,hold.
''               And DRIVER_REV 40's unbiased current (getCurrent() adds the reading's half count; the rest zero is
''               the offset rounded, up to 1 mV above the truncated mean): every bound on getCurrent() or the rest
''               zero re-checked, none moved. R16-T0-RESTZERO's +/-10 mA now states its terms (at SF_REST_LO): the
''               rest reading is centred on 0 (was 0 .. +1 mV), 89 of 100 at worst on Rev B, and the band holds
''               only on Rev B. T0-27's net_max_mv nets the driver's own zero, so it reads what the fold compares.
''               No record or cell changes.
''               27 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV 27 (DRIVER_REV 46, PL-160 owner Q3): setRampingValues() and
''               getRampingValues() are gone from the library. Every read of the four driver limits is now the
''               TESTING USE testGetRampLimits() (same four, same order); every restore of the ramp is
''               setAcceleration() / setDeceleration() of the rates read before (the same rate gives the same step,
''               so the restored limits are exact, and T0-5 now also judges that). R20-T0-API-ACCEL loses its three
''               raw rows (setRampingValues.raw, .min0, .cap) and T0A_RAW_UP / T0A_RAW_DN with them.
''               27 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV 28: three instrument defects the release-candidate pass found (no driver
''               change). (1) ATLIMIT's negative leg arms its own T0_25_NEG_LIMIT_MS (1_000, DERIVED at the constant):
''               the 300 ms limit fired ~90 ms into the drive, before the negative's stopMotor(), because a time limit
''               now fires when the driver's stop plan reaches its deadline -- R20-T0-SR-ATLIMIT and -EV-STOP read
''               42 where 41 was the design's. (2) A stop's landing pass is judged by the step it took (-vPrev) and
''               then its end at rest, not by the a = 0 jerkStep publishes on that pass -- RAMP-SHAPE's stops and
''               RAMP-UNWIND scored |aPrev| (189, 136) as one jerk. (3) The target is read SIGNX 30, as gettgtincr
''               reads it: bit 31 is the sync flag, so the reversal's -40_075_744 read +2_107_407_904 and REVERSE
''               could never arrive (NOMEAS).
''               30 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV 29: T0-27 (tier t0-reva) for the Rev A platform, with no window (Stephen,
''               2026-09-30: "Prepare it to run on the RevA platform that has two RevA boards"; boards are never moved
''               between platforms; R1 no PLOT windows in testing; R3 a 10 s lead-in; R14 the grip is held until the
''               program stops the wheel). A T0_27_LEAD_IN_MS (10 s) lead-in in which nothing moves; then BOTH groups
''               start, LEFT then RIGHT, each printing T0-27,board, and a group not reading REV_A is printed as a finding
''               and not driven (it had stopped at the first REV_A, assuming one swapped board). The two unloaded legs
''               run on EACH Rev A group (R22-T0-REVA-FOLD over up to four legs). The positive control lost its t0reva
''               PLOT window and its SPACE key (bT0vWaitSpace() and the T0_27_KEY_* constants are gone): the RIGHT's
''               power-5 leg runs straight on to T0_27_POWER_HOLD, so the wheel speeds up while turning -- his cue to
''               grip and hold -- and the judged window opens T0_27_GRIP_LEAD_MS (3 s) later. REVA-FOLD's criterion
''               token names the threshold it judges, NO_FOLD_UNDER_5MV_NET (was NO_FOLD_2A_AT_DUTY_FLOOR). Records:
''               T0-27,begin gains grip_lead_ms and net_fold_mv; T0-27,hold's key field becomes grip_lead_ms;
''               T0-27,hold,prompt is gone (plain operator lines replace it); T0-27,end gains rev_a_groups.
''               30 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV 30: three findings of the first Rev A platform run (REVA-PLATFORM-EVALUATION.md,
''               debug_260930-155650.log), before Stephen reruns it after checking the LEFT motor's leads. (1) A refused
''               start said the group "read NONE, not a ready REV_A board"; it now says the START CHECK refused it and
''               with which checks, and three new T0-27,probe records print what each lead probe read (testGetProbe(),
''               readable after a refusal), so an open lead can be told from a false refusal. (2) REVA-FOLDPOS could not
''               measure: a firm grip latched the protective stop inside the 3 s lead, the window then saw a secured
''               bridge, its duty gate was unreachable under the fold, and noise folds (68-81 a second unloaded) made
''               "the fold rose" meaningless. It is now HANDS-OFF (Stephen, 2026-09-30: the tests run without him
''               interceding): after each Rev A group's legs, a hard speed-up from rest (ACCEL_MAX_MM_S2 to
''               T0_27_POWER_KICK, t0vKickLeg()) loads the link with acceleration current; PASS is a fold rate of
''               twice the group's own unloaded legs' rate (crit KICK_FOLD_RATE_2X, was HELD_FOLDS_ON_5MV), NOMEAS
''               when the speed-up did not load the link (a mean net reading under T0_27_KICK_MEAN_MV). The grip, its
''               cue lines, t0vHoldLeg() and the legs' hand-off into it are gone; both groups get a positive control,
''               each its own SIGNOFF. (3) The kick records print the stop reason. Records: T0-27,probe new;
''               T0-27,begin loses power_hold and grip_lead_ms, gains power_kick, kick_win_ms, kick_mean_mv and
''               pos_rate_x100; T0-27,hold / holdsense become T0-27,kick / kicksense (rate_x100, ref_x100,
''               net_mean_mv, driven_ms, stop_reason; no duty_gate, fold_ramp or grip fields).
''               01 Oct 2026 -- SRC_REV 31: booleans print as words (PL-23). T0-20's rev_b and the T0-24 try row's
''               in_band, band_entered, shorted and estop_latched print TRUE/FALSE; its measured prints TRUE, FALSE or
''               CUT (a DONE / ABORT cut the try).
''               01 Oct 2026 -- SRC_REV 32: the banner prints the commit after src_rev (PL-68): the short SHA in a
''               bench pack, NOT_A_PACK from the source tree (isp_bench_commit.spin2).
''
'' =================================================================================================

{ Rig: the dual 6.5" platform -- two Rev B boards, 18.5V pack.

  BUILD WITH -D BENCH_CFG. That selects isp_bldc_motor_userconfig_bench.spin2,
  a peer config file stating the bench and nothing else, in place of
  isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2. Nobody has to activate a block, and the
  file end users edit is neither read nor written by a bench run:

      pnut-ts -l -d -D BENCH_CFG test_bench_t0.spin2

  It still compiles without the flag -- build-check.sh does exactly that --
  against whichever user block is active. Under a block with
  WHEEL_DIA_IN_INCH = 0.0 the T0-3 and T0-6 distance conversions correctly
  report themselves unavailable rather than returning a tick count.

  Every test below calls testSetup(), which runs the whole of init() -- board
  detection, constant derivation, power tables, unit conversion -- WITHOUT
  starting a driver cog, so the motor rail can stay off and the motor can stay
  unplugged. The exceptions are T0-10 (needs a real, running driver cog so the
  fourth ADC channel is actively calibrated and frame-locked; it still
  commands zero speed, so nothing turns), T0-11 (five real start()/stop()
  cycles reading live telemetry at zero command), T0-13 (a real start() held
  at zero command for 1000 ms), T0-14b (a real start()/stop() cycle to prove
  the post-stop board-type read stays clean), T0-15 (start()/stop() cycles
  probing cog accounting), T0-3 (a stop limit is accepted only by a started
  motor), and T0-17, T0-19, T0-20 and T0-22 (the 6.0.0 start, steering-start,
  rest-zero and front-cog-failure cells). Keep the motor rail on for all of
  these; none of them ever commands nonzero speed.

  Output: one tagged line per data point, "T0-n,field,value,...", on the plain
  debug stream. Sign-off records ("SIGNOFF-DECL,..." / "SIGNOFF,...") are a
  second, separately-tagged stream, read from the log into each visit's
  analysis report (design DOCs/plans/VISIT-SIGNOFF-DESIGN.md).

  TRAPS (task 3539, PL-44/PL-47): a `\`-trap is an exceptional-return-path
  device, not a routine way to capture a normal result (STEPHEN: "traps are
  an exeptional return path - not normal use"). Since the 6.0.0 error contract
  (tasks 3554/3555) the library aborts nowhere: every command returns a status
  (0 or a negative ERR_*) and records it for getError(), and start()/startEx()
  return the cog id 0..7 or -1 with the cause in getError(). So every call below
  is UNTRAPPED and judged by its returned value and getError().

  ONE top-level trap covers the whole suite: main() calls `\runTier0Tests()`
  and prints its trapped value on EVERY run, so an abort nothing anticipated
  still shows up instead of silently ending the session. A testT0_n() that goes
  silent under such an abort skips its own SIGNOFF lines, and any declared cell
  with no verdict is NOMEAS by the host's convention (reason NOT_REACHED).

  T0-1's six derived constants (dead_gap, pwm_limit, duty_min, duty_max,
  adc_fram, frame_cnt) and T0-3 (finding F) both read via two new TEST-USE
  ONLY getters on isp_bldc_motor.spin2: testGetDriveConstants() and
  testGetStopHallTicks(). Both are pure read-only snapshots.

  Every start() here, the steering start included, commands zero speed, so
  nothing turns. If anything behaves unexpectedly: physical battery
  disconnect. emergencyCutoff() latches until clearEmergency() since task
  3556 (S-4 retired), but it is a software stop, not a panic button.

  T0-12 (hand-rotation anchor) is deliberately NOT part of this unattended
  run. It is compiled in only under -D T0_HAND, has its own bench-run.sh tier
  (t0-hand), waits on an operator keypress rather than a timer, and carries
  no sign-off cell.
}

' T0_OWN_TIER is set by every build that runs one test of its own (T0_HAND, T0_STOPMODE, T0_STOPREASON, T0_API). It
' COMPILES OUT every unattended test body, not just its call: a call gated at run time still compiles its debug()
' records, and this binary's DEBUG data has a hard end. Any record whose bytes lie past image offset 13,684 is cut
' at that byte or never sent -- measured three times: 2026-09-20 t0-hand's PLOT create stopped at
' "hand-rotation an", t0's "T0-23,begin,no_bo" (PL-94) stopped at the same offset, and 2026-09-22's
' USB captures carried no display command at all (P2-HAZARD-REGISTER DBG-1, DBG-16). Gating the bodies
' takes t0-hand's DEBUG footprint from 15,674 to about 7,250 bytes, and changes nothing it prints.
' (Named T0_ATTENDED until task 3621: T0_STOPREASON runs its own test unattended, so "attended" no longer said it.)
' SRC_REV 26: T0_REVA (tier t0-reva, T0-27, PL-163) is one more.
#ifdef T0_REVA
#define T0_OWN_TIER
#endif
#ifdef T0_HAND
#define T0_OWN_TIER
#endif
#ifdef T0_STOPMODE
#define T0_OWN_TIER
#endif
#ifdef T0_STOPREASON
#define T0_OWN_TIER
#endif
#ifdef T0_API
#define T0_OWN_TIER
#endif

' Select the two-wheel configuration in isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2 (a -D BENCH_CFG build uses the bench file instead)
#DEFINE CFG_DUAL_MOTOR
#IFDEF __PNUT_TS__
#PRAGMA EXPORTDEF CFG_DUAL_MOTOR
#ENDIF

CON { bench target }

' Which motor this harness talks to. Deliberately NOT read from the user
' config: a dual-motor block defines LEFT_MOTOR_BASE and RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE and
' no ONLY_MOTOR_BASE at all, so reading that user constant will not COMPILE on
' a dual bench -- which is what the real bench is (dual 6.5" wheels, Rev B
' boards, 18.5V pack). PINS_P16_P31 is a real motor under every config block
' in isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2: the right wheel on the dual 6.5"/18.5V
' block, the left wheel on the alternate dual block, and the sole motor on
' every single-motor block. Everything else -- motor type, drive voltage,
' wheel diameter -- still comes from whichever block is active, so the harness
' describes the hardware the operator says is connected.
    T0_MOTOR_BASE = motor.PINS_P16_P31

' Second populated base for T0-14's board-detection sweeps (R2-T0-REPEAT,
' R2-T0-DIRTY). PINS_P32_P47 is a legal enum value under every config block
' regardless of which is active, so this compiles everywhere; it is only
' actually wired to a second board on the dual-motor bench. Using the raw
' PINS_* enum (not user.LEFT_MOTOR_BASE) sidesteps the same single-motor
' compile hazard T0_MOTOR_BASE's comment above describes.
    T0_SECOND_BASE = motor.PINS_P32_P47

CON { build identity }

    SRC_REV = 32                                     ' hand-bumped whenever this file changes; printed in the banner

CON { timing }

    CLK_FREQ = 270_000_000                                      ' matches the audit's worked dead_gap example
    _clkfreq = CLK_FREQ
    READY_WAIT_MS  = 2_000                                      ' bound on a started driver reporting ready
    READY_POLL_MS  = 10

CON { 6.0.0 cells (task 3560) }

    BAD_PIN_BASE     = 99                                       ' not a PINS_* value: start() must reject it before any cog or pin is touched
    PL48_MARK_BASE   = 8                                        ' P8..P15: the release demo's HDMI group (PL-48)
    PL48_MARK_SPAN   = 7                                        ' addpins operand: 8 pins
    PL48_MARK_MASK   = $FF                                      ' DIRA bits 8..15, shifted down
    PL48_MARK_SHIFT  = 8
    SF_START_COGS    = 2                                        ' DERIVED -- task 3513: a single-motor start() is the driver plus its front cog
    SF_STEER_COGS    = 3                                        ' DERIVED -- task 3513: two owned drivers plus the steering front cog
    REST_SAMPLES     = 50                                       ' R16-T0-RESTZERO: getCurrent() reads averaged per board
    REST_SAMPLE_MS   = 20
    SF_REST_LO       = -100                                     ' DERIVED -- +/-10 mA (0.1 mA units); unfixed LEFT read ~535 (PL-45, Visit 1)
    SF_REST_HI       = 100
' SF_REST_LO .. SF_REST_HI, its terms (SRC_REV 26 extended, DRIVER_REV 40), on Rev B (150 mV/A: 1 mV of sense is 66.7
'  units). At rest getCurrent() reads the rest zero's own rounding: DRIVER_REV 40's zero is the offset rounded
'  (restZeroFinish()) and the reading adds back its half count, so its mean is within 0.5 mV of 0: 33 units. (Until
'  DRIVER_REV 40 it was 0 .. 1 mV for a zero at or above 0, the zero then the truncated mean: 0 .. 67.) Random terms,
'  on the library's own noise premise (sigma <= 1.73 mV a reading, FOLD_MIN_MV's note): the zero's 200-reading mean,
'  0.12 mV (8 units), and this cell's REST_SAMPLES mean, 0.245 mV (16); 3 sigma of both together is 54. Each reading's
'  divide and the mean's truncate less than 1 unit each. 33 + 54 + 2 = 89, inside 100, so a correct Rev B driver
'  passes. REV B ONLY: on Rev A (5 mV/A) one mV is 2_000 units, so the zero's rounding alone reaches 1_000 and a
'  correct Rev A driver would fail this band by construction, so on any board but Rev B the cell is NOMEAS (the
'  board is read from getBoardType(), the revision the running driver recorded).

CON { API promise and regression cells (tasks 3577, 3574) }

' R17-T0-ACCEL (SRC_REV 25, DRIVER_REV 38): setAcceleration() sets the speed-up acceleration LIMIT, testGetRampLimits()'s
'  maxRamp, and its jerk, minRamp (PL-160). DERIVED, not read from the library: one step per drive pass is
'  0.0294485 mm/s^2 at the rim of the 6.5in wheel (44_000 / 23 = 1_913.04 passes/s, squared, x 6 ticks per electrical
'  cycle x 5.76 mm per tick / 2^32 per cycle), so 1_000 mm/s^2 is 33_957.6 steps, 33_958. setAcceleration(
'  ACCEL_ANCHOR_MM_S2) must land within 1% of it: a factor wrong anywhere in the conversion moves it far outside that.
'  The bench's wheel only (BENCH_CFG), as the anchor before it was. The anchor is NOT the built-in rate
'  (ACCEL_BUILTIN_MM_S2), whose step the library converts with the same code, so it could not catch that code.
    ACCEL_ANCHOR_MM_S2 = 1_000
    ACCEL_ANCHOR_STEP  = 33_958                                 ' DERIVED above, the 6.5in wheel
    ACCEL_ANCHOR_TOL_DIV = 100                                  ' 1% of it
    ACCEL_BELOW_RANGE  = -1                                     ' a negative rate, as well as the one just below range
' R17-T0-KMMI: exact unit identities the conversion must reproduce tick for tick
    M_PER_KM           = 1_000
    FT_PER_MI          = 5_280
' R17-T0-VOLTGET: the bench pack's nominal voltage (the bench config's PWR_18p5V, the 5S pack -- STEPHEN
'  2026-09-17, "18.5 V nominal 5S"). The harness is built with -D BENCH_CFG, so that is the voltage start() gets.
    SF_PACK_MV         = 18_500
' R17-T0-DEADGAP (task 3574, A1 / PL-9): both 64010 manuals' minimum commutation dead gap, either board
    DEADTIME_MIN_NS    = 250
    HZ_PER_MHZ         = 1_000_000
    NS_PER_US          = 1_000
' each cell's n: the claims its one verdict covers
    DEADGAP_READS_JUDGED = 1
    ACCEL_CALLS_JUDGED = 5                                      ' three refusals, the anchor, the top rate
    KMMI_CLAIMS_JUDGED = 3                                      ' km conversion, mi conversion, the refusal
    VOLT_READS_JUDGED  = 3                                      ' motor, steering running, steering not started

CON { cog-exhaustion probe (T0-8, T0-15) }

    MAX_SPACER_COGS   = 7                                       ' every cog besides this harness's own
    SPACER_STACK_LONGS = 32                                     ' generous headroom for a trivial idle loop

CON { stop reasons and the event log (T0-25, -D T0_STOPREASON only; task 3621, DRIVER-REPORTING-DESIGN.md SS6) }

' The RIGHT wheel (T0_MOTOR_BASE) is driven at T0_25_POWER, wheels up, and stopped each way a program can stop it.
'  Each value is the design's pre-registered one (SS6), not tuned here.
    T0_25_POWER         = 15                                    ' every drive in T0-25
    T0_25_RUN_MS        = 300                                   ' a leg drives this long before its stop
    T0_25_STICKY_MS     = 500                                   ' COMMANDED: the reason still reads the same this much later
    T0_25_LIMIT_MS      = 300                                   ' ATLIMIT: stopAfterTime()'s limit, DTU_MILLISEC
    T0_25_EARLY_MS      = 100                                   ' ATLIMIT's negative: stopMotor() this soon, the limit still armed
    ' SRC_REV 28: the negative's own limit. DRIVER_REV 38/39 fire a time limit when the driver's own stop plan reaches
    '  the deadline, so a 300 ms limit fires ~90 ms into a power-15 drive (from 100 ms in, the stop takes ~220 ms: the
    '  unwind of the rising acceleration, then the S-curve down), BEFORE the negative's stopMotor() -- pass RC read
    '  SR_AT_LIMIT there. DERIVED bound: the longest stop from a power-15 drive is the unwind (A / Jx = 327 passes, 171 ms)
    '  plus the triangular stop from its speed (2 sqrt(v / J) = 843 passes, 441 ms at 18.5 x 10^6) -- ~612 ms -- plus
    '  the plan's early bias (~4 ms). A 1_000 ms limit therefore cannot fire before ~384 ms, well after T0_25_EARLY_MS.
    T0_25_NEG_LIMIT_MS  = 1_000
    T0_25_TIMEOUT_MS    = 100                                   ' LINKLOST: setCommandTimeout()
    T0_25_SILENT_MS     = 400                                   ' ...and no command for this long
    T0_25_REFRESH_MS    = 30                                    ' LINKLOST's negative: the drive re-sent this often, for T0_25_SILENT_MS
    T0_25_REST_MS       = 3_000                                 ' bound on the driver reading DCS_STOPPED after a stop
    T0_25_EV_STOPS      = 7                                     ' EV-STOP: the stops the SR legs record, in order (t0rWantStop())
    T0_25_CYCLES        = 20                                    ' EV-LOST: drive/stop cycles with nothing read
    T0_25_CYCLE_MS      = 60                                    ' each cycle's drive, and its pause after the stop
    T0_25_COG_CYCLES    = 4                                     ' EV-2COG: the stops both reading cogs must each read
    T0_25_HELPER_STACK  = 128                                   ' the helper reader cog: getEvent() and its callee, with headroom
    T0_25_HANDSHAKE_MS  = 2_000                                 ' bound on each of the helper cog's two handshakes
    T0_25_DRAIN_MAX     = 40                                    ' bound on one drain: EV_QUEUE_DEPTH + EV_LOST + what arrives meanwhile
    T0_25_REC_GAP_MS    = 10_000                                ' PL-120: after a refused RIGHT, one start of it every this often...
    T0_25_REC_MAX_MS    = 180_000                               ' ...until it starts or this long after the refusal

' PL-151 (SRC_REV 21): R20-T0-ROTSTOP and R20-T0-ESTOPSTATUS, run after the eight cells above (t0rRotStop(),
'  t0rEstopStatus()), so their stops fall after EV-STOP's read and after EV-TOTAL's count.
    T0_25_ROT_TURNS     = 1                                     ' ROTSTOP: stopAfterRotation(1, DRU_ROTATIONS) -- 90 ticks on the 6.5" wheel
    T0_25_ROT_WAIT_MS   = 10_000                                ' bound on the limit firing: 90 ticks at power 15 (~59 ticks/s,
                                                                '  isp_bldc_motor's 49 at an eighth and 98 at a quarter) is ~1.5 s + the ramp
    T0_25_ROT_NEG_EXTRA_MS = 1_000                              ' the negative drives the positive's fire time plus this: ~59 more
                                                                '  ticks, so a wheel nothing stopped is well past the limit
  ' ROTSTOP's tolerance on the tracked ticks at rest against the limit. DERIVED from the stop's own logic
  '  (isp_bldc_motor bFrontLimitsDue()): the stop is written in the first 1 ms front pass where
  '  the travel since arming + frontStopTicks() >= the limit. frontStopTicks() is the FIELD's jerk-limited stop in
  '  closed form, floored to a whole tick; the rotor follows the field, not exactly, and the library states the
  '  result as "at rest at the limit (within about two hall ticks)" (stopAfterRotation()'s doc) -- 2 ticks. Plus one
  '  hall tick: the travel counts whole ticks, so the crossing is seen up to one tick late -- 3 in all, either side.
  '  At ~59 ticks/s a 1 ms pass carries ~0.06 ticks, so the pass cadence adds nothing further. SRC_REV 25: the plan is
  '  the jerk-limited stop's (DRIVER_REV 38's front-cog stopPlan(), exact; DRIVER_REV 39's the driver's own, which
  '  over-states the stop by its age and its take-pass case, so a stop may rest short by T0_25_PLAN_EARLY_TICKS more):
  '  -(T0_25_ROT_TOL_TICKS + T0_25_PLAN_EARLY_TICKS) .. +T0_25_ROT_TOL_TICKS, -4 .. +3. (Before DRIVER_REV 38 the plan
  '  was the stepped ramp-down's, incr x (incr / ramp_down + 1) / 2, and the band +/- 3.)
    T0_25_ROT_TOL_TICKS = 3

' SRC_REV 22 (DRIVER_REV 33): R20-T0-ODOMETER, R20-T0-MOVEDONE and R20-T0-PERSIST, run after R20-T0-ESTOPSTATUS (t0rOdometer(),
'  t0rPersist()). Their stops fall after every event read, as ROTSTOP's do.
    T0_25_ODO_CM        = 30                                    ' ODOMETER: each driveForDistance(): 52 ticks on the 6.5" wheel (5.76 mm
                                                                '  a tick), about a second at T0_25_POWER -- past its ramps: SRC_REV 25
                                                                '  (DRIVER_REV 38), ~18 ticks to reach 23.4 x 10^6 and ~15 to stop from it
    T0_25_ODO_WAIT_MS   = 10_000                                ' bound on each move ending (isMoveDone())
    T0_25_ESTOP_HOLD_MS = 100                                   ' the e-stop is held this long: 100 front passes, EACH of which zeroed
                                                                '  the pre-33 odometer (frontTrack()), so one pass would do
    T0_25_PERSIST_SPEED = 40                                    ' PERSIST: setMaxSpeed() with the motor stopped -- not the default 75
    T0_25_PERSIST_DIST  = 30                                    ' ...setMaxSpeedForDistance(), likewise, and different from the first
    T0_25_HOLD_ARM_MS   = 500                                   ' bound on the restarted motor's hold reading HS_HOLDING: the front cog
                                                                '  arms it on its first pass at rest, so ~1 ms; 500 is margin

' SRC_REV 25 (DRIVER_REV 38, PL-160): the jerk-limited generator's cells (t0rRamp()), run after R20-T0-MOVEDONE and before
'  R20-T0-PERSIST, which restarts the motor. Their stops are EV_STOP events nothing reads, after every read. Two powers:
'  at 18.5 V on the 6.5in wheel incrementForPower() gives 81_717_144 (50) and 40_075_744 (25), 218 and 107 ticks/s. A
'  ramp holds its acceleration limit A (at jerk J) only when it changes the speed by more than A^2 / J -- 16.2 x 10^6
'  speeding up (33_958^2 / 71) and 24.0 x 10^6 slowing (49_918^2 / 104) on the built-in rates -- and every ramp below
'  changes it by 40 x 10^6 or more, so each reaches its limit and holds it for a while.
    T0_25_RAMP_HI       = 50                                    ' the upper power
    T0_25_RAMP_LO       = 25                                    ' the lower power, and the reversal's
    T0_25_RAMP_WAIT_MS  = 5_000                                 ' bound on one watch: the longest ramp, rest to T0_25_RAMP_HI, is
                                                                '  A / J passes in, 1_928 at A and A / J out, ~2_885 passes (1.5 s)
    T0_25_SETTLE_MS     = 100                                   ' watched at the target after arriving: ~190 passes, a = 0 on each
    T0_25_MIN_JUDGED    = 100                                   ' a watch that judged fewer pairs of passes is NOMEAS
    T0_25_WATCH_STACK   = 128                                   ' the sampler cog: t0pWatch() and its three callees, no library call
    T0P_IDLE_US         = 100                                   ' the sampler cog's poll for its next watch
  ' THE SAMPLER (t0pWatch(), on its own cog so that it is watching BEFORE cog 0 sends the command it judges) reads the
  '  driver's status run directly, by its hub offsets from @drive_u (isp_bldc_motor VAR order, testGetAbiAddrs()), and the
  '  launch run's target. A loop is a handful of hub reads and no method call, a few microseconds against a 522.7 us drive
  '  pass (each watch prints gap_pk_us, its worst). A sample whose two reads of v differ straddled the driver's status
  '  write and is skipped. A new pass is a sample whose v or a differs from the last; it is JUDGED with the last only when
  '  the two good samples were under T0R_PASS_GAP_US apart, so no pass can lie between them, and only when its v changed
  '  by its own a (v' = v + a'; the pass that reaches rest, v and a both 0, excepted). Anything else is counted, never
  '  judged: unres (the gap) or incons (a change of v the generator did not make -- the hold decay). A pass whose v and a
  '  both repeat the last is the generator at rest or at speed (a = 0 both times), so no judged step can hide in one.
    T0R_ST_POS          = 8                                     ' pos
    T0R_ST_STATE        = 13                                    ' drv_state
    T0R_ST_INCR         = 16                                    ' drv_incr_now: v
    T0R_ST_LAGHELD      = 17                                    ' lag_held
    T0R_ST_ACCEL        = motor.DRVR_STATUS_ACCEL_NOW_IDX       ' drv_accel_now: a (21), after foldback_frames; the library's own
                                                                '  index (DRIVER_REV 39: no longer the run's last long)
    T0R_LN_TARGET       = 3                                     ' targetIncre, from @pinbase: the command the driver takes
    T0R_PASS_GAP_US     = motor.DRIVE_PASS_US - 1               ' 522 us, under one drive pass (522.7 us)
    T0R_US_PER_S        = 1_000_000
    T0R_MS_PER_S        = 1_000
  ' t0pWatch()'s modes: T0W_ARRIVE ends a watch T0_25_SETTLE_MS after v first reads the target, T0W_REST at DCS_STOPPED
    #0, T0W_ARRIVE, T0W_REST
  ' The stop plan's legs (t0rPlanLeg()). CRUISE: armed at T0_25_RAMP_HI's steady speed. MID-RAMP: armed at rest, then that
  '  drive, so each fires while the speed-up still holds its limit (DERIVED, desk: it holds it from about 8 x 10^6 to 74 x
  '  10^6; 90 ticks fires near 33 x 10^6, 600 mm (104 ticks) near 41 x 10^6, 1_600 ms near 38 x 10^6). A leg whose stop
  '  is read at speed or at rest instead is NOMEAS: it did not test a stop from mid-ramp.
    T0_25_PLAN_ROT_C    = 2                                     ' CRUISE: stopAfterRotation(2, DRU_ROTATIONS), 180 ticks; the stop
                                                                '  from 81.7 x 10^6 runs ~121, so it fires ~0.27 s after arming
    T0_25_PLAN_MS_C     = 1_500                                 ' CRUISE: stopAfterTime(), ms; the stop takes ~1_108 ms (2_118 passes)
    T0_25_PLAN_MM_M     = 600                                   ' MID-RAMP: stopAfterDistance(600, DDU_MM)
    T0_25_PLAN_ROT_M    = 1                                     ' MID-RAMP: stopAfterRotation(1, DRU_ROTATIONS), 90 ticks
    T0_25_PLAN_MS_M     = 1_600                                 ' MID-RAMP: stopAfterTime(), ms
    #0, T0P_LEG_ROT_C, T0P_LEG_MS_C, T0P_LEG_MM_M, T0P_LEG_ROT_M, T0P_LEG_MS_M
    T0P_LEGS            = T0P_LEG_MS_M + 1
  ' A distance leg's tolerance is ROTSTOP's (T0_25_ROT_TOL_TICKS late, and T0_25_PLAN_EARLY_TICKS more early), plus
  '  T0_25_ARM_SKEW_TICKS either way for a limit armed at speed: the harness reads the position just before the call
  '  and the front cog takes its own base a pass later, so a hall edge may fall between the two.
    T0_25_ARM_SKEW_TICKS = 1
  ' A time leg's band on (the field at zero) - (the deadline), ms, DERIVED as test_bench_dual's TIMESTOP band is, for
  '  this sampler (microseconds, where TIMESTOP polls every ms). THE PLAN (DRIVER_REV 39, PL-161): the DRIVER publishes
  '  its own stop plan about 232 us after each pass k (ten PWM frames): P passes counted from T_k, the largest of three
  '  cases -- the stop taken by pass k + 1, or by k + 2 after a take pass whose acceleration is either end of
  '  [a - Jx, a + Jx] (any command, any lag gate) -- and frontStopMs() is S = floor(P x 523 / 1_000) + 1. The field's
  '  zero, at most T_k + P x 522.7 us, is therefore never after the fire instant + S: the plan is never late by
  '  construction, and it runs early by what it over-states.
  '  LATE: the limit is tested once a front pass against a getms() part-way through it, 2 x 1_000 / FRONT_LOOP_HZ; the
  '   harness takes its deadline before the call, up to 1 ms before the library's own, 1; the zero instant is carried
  '   from getct() to getms(), which truncates, 1. Total 4. (DRIVER_REV 38's front-cog plan also needed one pass for a
  '   stop taken a pass beyond the state it read; DRIVER_REV 39's take-pass case covers that.)
  '  EARLY: S is rounded up by up to 1 ms, 1; P may exceed the stop the field takes by the take pass and the +Jx end's
  '   extra unwind pass and speed, three passes at most, 2 (1.57 ms); the plan's age -- counted from T_k, read up to
  '   232 + 523 us later -- 1 (0.76 ms); DRIVE_PASS_US (523) overstates 522.7 us by under 1 ms for any stop under 3_333
  '   passes, 1; the reading's getms() truncates, 1. Total 6 (4.9 in exact terms from 81.7 x 10^6 at the built-in
  '   rates, of which the plan's own three -- rounding, extra passes, age -- are 3.3).
    T0_25_TIME_LATE_MS  = 2 * (T0R_MS_PER_S / motor.FRONT_LOOP_HZ) + 1 + 1
    T0_25_TIME_EARLY_MS = 1 + 2 + 1 + 1 + 1
  ' The distance plan's over-statement (DRIVER_REV 39), the early side of every distance limit in T0-25 (ROTSTOP, ODOMETER,
  '  the STOPPLAN tick legs): the published travel is the largest of the same three cases, counted from pass k's field,
  '  so a stop rests short of its limit by at most the travel of the plan's age and of its three extra passes -- (0.76 +
  '  1.57) ms of travel, 0.15 tick at T0_25_POWER's ~62 ticks/s and 0.51 tick at T0_25_RAMP_HI's 218: one whole tick.
    T0_25_PLAN_EARLY_TICKS = 1

' SRC_REV 26 (DRIVER_REV 39, PL-161): R22-T0-FRAMESLACK and its FRAME WATCHER (t0fWatch(), a cog of its own, started and
'  stopped with the sampler, so it covers every drive, stop, reversal and mid-ramp limit stop t0rRamp() makes). DRIVER_REV
'  39 runs one stage of its stop planner (planStage) in each of the nine PWM frames after a drive pass, after that
'  frame's status write, in the frame's slack. Its failure is a frame whose work runs past the next ADC sample: an
'  overrun, or, a whole frame late, a lost ADC sample.
'  WHAT THE DRIVER PUBLISHES: loop_ticks (loop_dtcks_) is one control frame's time from its start -- BEFORE it waits for
'   its ADC sample (wait4adc) -- to the end of its own work W: its ADC wait plus W. Whatever ran between the previous
'   frame's work and this frame's start -- that frame's status write, a planner stage, or the drive pass -- came out of
'   this frame's wait: loop_ticks = frame_cnt - (the previous frame's work, its write, and its stage or drive pass) + W.
'  THE NEGATIVE, what an overrun reads: the sample is already waiting, the wait is ~0, so loop_ticks is the frame's own
'   work alone, at most T0F_WORK_MAX_CLK. A lost sample is an overrun of more than a frame and reads the same.
'  THE CRITERION: the least loop_ticks of the watch is above T0F_WORK_MAX_CLK, so every frame's ADC wait was positive --
'   no frame ran past its sample. T0F_WORK_MAX_CLK is PL-161's bound on one control frame's own work, 699 clocks
'   (frame_clocks.py: every branch counted taken, 2 clocks an instruction), a count that does not scale with the clock.
'   The frame is frame_cnt clocks, clkfreq / PWM_RATE_IN_HZ (6_136 at 270 MHz), read from the driver itself
'   (testGetDriveConstants()). T0-25,frame prints frame_cnt - least + T0F_WORK_MAX_CLK, the most any frame can have
'   used. EXPECTED at 270 MHz (PL-161's DERIVED stage costs): the least is a frame after a planner stage, stage 9's
'   1_750 clocks the worst, so about 6_136 - 1_750 - the status write, ~4_350; a drive pass (<= 1_184) leaves ~4_900.
'  MEASURED ONLY WHEN EVERY FRAME WAS READ, AND DRIVING WAS WATCHED: a loop_ticks value stands from one status write to
'   the next, which are at least frame_cnt - T0F_WORK_MAX_CLK apart when no frame overruns (an overrun's own reading
'   stands until the next frame's write, all but a whole frame later), so a watch whose largest gap between two reads
'   is under that read every frame's value; and the watch must have covered driving -- the SHAPE watches or a mid-ramp
'   limit stop measured (the planner's stages cost most with v and a both non-zero).
    T0R_ST_LOOP         = 11                                    ' loop_ticks (loop_dtcks_): a control frame's ADC wait + its own work
    T0F_WORK_MAX_CLK    = 699                                   ' PL-161's bound on one control frame's own work, clocks
    T0F_STACK           = 48                                    ' the frame watcher's cog: one method, a few locals, no call
    T0F_PARK_MS         = 100                                   ' the frame watcher's idle once its readings are posted

  ' T0-25's seven stop legs, run in this order (t0rLeg()); each reads getStopReason() as its drive opens, after its stop,
  '  and once more after the leg's own later act:
  '  T0R_LEG_CMD       - stopMotor() after T0_25_RUN_MS: SR_COMMANDED, and still SR_COMMANDED T0_25_STICKY_MS later
  '  T0R_LEG_LIMIT     - stopAfterTime(T0_25_LIMIT_MS) armed, then the drive: the limit stops it, SR_AT_LIMIT
  '  T0R_LEG_LIMIT_NEG - the same limit armed, stopMotor() at T0_25_EARLY_MS: SR_COMMANDED, and still so once the
  '                      limit's deadline has passed at rest (a limit firing with no drive open records nothing)
  '  T0R_LEG_ESTOP     - emergencyCutoff() at speed: SR_EMERGENCY, and still so after clearEmergency()
  '  T0R_LEG_ESTOP_NEG - stopMotor(), rest, then emergencyCutoff() AT REST: SR_COMMANDED both times (first cause wins)
  '  T0R_LEG_LINK      - setCommandTimeout(T0_25_TIMEOUT_MS), the drive, then no command for T0_25_SILENT_MS: SR_LINK_LOST
  '  T0R_LEG_LINK_NEG  - the same timeout, the drive re-sent every T0_25_REFRESH_MS for T0_25_SILENT_MS (the drive still
  '                      open, SR_NONE), then stopMotor(): SR_COMMANDED; the timeout is turned off again
    #0, T0R_LEG_CMD, T0R_LEG_LIMIT, T0R_LEG_LIMIT_NEG, T0R_LEG_ESTOP, T0R_LEG_ESTOP_NEG, T0R_LEG_LINK, T0R_LEG_LINK_NEG
    T0R_LEGS            = T0R_LEG_LINK_NEG + 1

CON { hand-rotation anchor (T0-12, -D T0_HAND only) }

    T0_12_HALL_OFFSET = 5                                       ' pin_hall_u is base+5; hall inputs are base+5..base+7
    T0_12_HALL_SPAN   = 2                                       ' addpins operand: three hall pins
    T0_12_POLL_MS     = 1                                       ' hall poll period while counting
    T0_12_KEY_POLLS   = 100                                     ' polls between keypress checks (~100 ms) -- matches
                                                                 ' PC_KEY's own ~100 ms keypress-latch window
                                                                 ' (DISPLAY-PATTERNS-builders-guide.md SS7)
    T0_12_PRINT_POLLS = 500                                     ' polls between progress lines AND panel redraws
                                                                 ' (~500 ms); the panel rides this existing cadence
                                                                 ' rather than adding a new one, so it costs nothing
                                                                 ' extra against the 1 ms hall poll (PL-42 fix)
    T0_12_KEY_WAIT_MS = 50                                      ' keypress poll period before counting starts
    T0_12_KEY_START   = "S"                                     ' starts the count (either case); no other key does
    T0_12_KEY_START_LC = "s"
    T0_12_KEY_STOP    = " "                                     ' SPACE stops the count; no other key does
    T0_12_REVOLUTIONS = 3                                       ' operator turns exactly this many full revolutions;
                                                                 ' baked into t0h_bg.bmp -- regenerate that asset
                                                                 ' (tools/gen_t0hand_assets.py) if this changes

' PL-39: the direction the operator is TOLD to turn, viewed from the hub side, is fixed at CW. The
' panel background bakes the instruction in (tools/gen_t0hand_assets.py), so a second direction
' would need a second asset set that could disagree with the log; instead one known direction plus
' the signed tick change (pos) is enough to tie the tick sign to the physical direction.
    T0_12_TOLD_CCW    = FALSE

